"""SuppTable_WB1_wholebrain_modulation_n288  -  Extent of whole-brain (217-node) edge-level modulation in each task condition and contrast

Computes
    Extent of whole-brain (217-node) edge-level modulation in each task
    condition and contrast: how many edges change, in which direction and how
    large the effect is.

Inputs
    06_upstream_inputs/whole_brain_fc_compare/model_data/wholebrain_results/{sst,mid}_data_{baseline,mani_ampa,mani_gaba}_217.mat  (fallback: /Users/yunman/Desktop/submission/revision/whole_brain_fc_compare/model_data/wholebrain_results/; not shipped in this package)
    06_upstream_inputs/empirical_simul_np_fcs_300subs/np_residualized_290subs.csv  (for the n=288 ID list)

Output
    $FIG4_OUT/figures/supp_wholebrain/wb_data/SuppTable_WB1_wholebrain_modulation_n288.csv  (default $FIG4_OUT = 03_analysis/fig4/_scratch)
    reference copy: 04_figures/supp_wholebrain/wb_data/SuppTable_WB1_wholebrain_modulation_n288.csv

Statistical tests
    Paired t test per edge over subjects with Benjamini-Hochberg FDR across the
    23,436 edges, and the distribution of within-subject Cohen's d_z.

Cohort
    n = 288 (the same exclusion as Fig. 4, applied to the 217-node whole-brain
    matrices).

Runs on a laptop
    partial - one or more inputs are not shipped in this package (listed under
    Inputs); with them present it runs on a laptop in seconds to a few minutes.

seed
    no random component

